  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level (3000) and comparing outcomes to it, then preferring the lottery with the higher probability of exceeding it. The individual does consider 3000 (as it appears in Lottery B), but not as a computed aspiration level from all outcomes. Instead, the individual focuses on the probability of winning any positive amount, treating 0 as the reference (not 3000). The justification is based on avoiding zero, not on exceeding a computed aspiration level. There is no mention of comparing outcomes to a mean of all outcomes or evaluating which lottery more often exceeds 3000. The reasoning process described is fundamentally different: it is based on ‘something vs. nothing’ rather than deviations from an aspiration level. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
}

